{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Hey, come on in. Good to see you both.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Hey.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Sorry we're late, uh, parking was a nightmare out there.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (DOCTOR): You're fine, don't worry. What brought you in today?",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): Cough.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (DOCTOR): Tell me about the cough.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): Mornings.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Every morning when he sits up. He'll hack for a good 20 minutes.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Does anything come up when you cough?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Brown.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Brown phlegm, pretty thick. I see it in the tissue every day.",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long has that morning cough been around?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Fifteen years, easy. It was already there when I started with him.",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (DOCTOR): You used to smoke, didn't you?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (DOCTOR): When did you quit?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): Last year.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Last March. A pack a day for forty years, then he stopped. He still wants one with his coffee, but he doesn't light it.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): A whole year off is a big deal. I'm really glad you stuck with it.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any chest pain when you cough, or just at rest?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Have you had any fevers?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Eh.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Has your weight changed at all?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Same.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Do you get short of breath?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Okay. What medicines are you on these days?",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (CAREGIVER): uh, just lisinerpril for his pressure. Ten milligrams... no, twenty milligrams, every morning.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): Lisinopril, twenty milligrams each morning. Anything besides that?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Nothing else. The blood pressure has been going on for years.",
  "[SEG0034] person_1 (DOCTOR): So high blood pressure, and we're still treating it. Let me listen to your lungs.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): Mm.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (DOCTOR): Deep breath. I hear a few wheezes at the bases, no crackles. Heart is regular.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): When you came up from the parking lot, um, how was the breathing?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): Winded.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): On the flat, or the stairs?",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Stairs.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'm thinking this is most likely chronic bronchitis from all those years of smoking, with the morning cough and the brown phlegm. I don't want to call it final until we measure your breathing.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'd like to get spirometry booked this week, the breathing test.",
  "[SEG0044] person_3 (CAREGIVER): I can bring him whenever.",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (DOCTOR): The front desk will set that up before you leave. With your smoking history, you should get the pneumococcal vaccine and a flu shot this season.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): Okay.",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (DOCTOR): Keep it up and stay off the cigarettes. If you cough up any blood, or the shortness of breath gets a lot worse, call us or go to the ER. Come back and see me in two weeks, once the spirometry is back, and we'll talk it through."
 ],
